stephen ryan wrote:
>
> Which weapon will incur more damage
>
> Being [Skilled] with a +2 dagger or [basic] with a "broad short sword"

Single hit or for the entire game?  Very different answers.

For a single hit, a dwarvish short sword will do more damage.

But for the entire game, short swords are poor weapons, there are no
short sword artifact weapons, and so advancing your skills in short
sword is almost always a waste of effort until you start playing style
games (ascending with an icebox to supply the demigod bar and such).

On the other hand, there are several types of daggers, there are
several dagger artifact weapons, you can put together a stack of
daggers for throwing, etc.

Once you get past a single hit, the beats the short sword nicely.
Unless you just threw your dagger at the monster and now you only
have the short sword.  Daggers are for throwing in addition to melee.

